WASH-SALE-AWARE SUBSTITUTE TEST -- real panel 2015-11-03..2026-11-11, BASE = live design + L1 (engine reproduces 53.0%/2.139).
Tax: $600k start book; ST 50.3% (37+13.3), LT 37.1% (20+3.8+13.3); netting + $3k ordinary offset + carryforward; tax paid each 15 Apr (first session on/after) from BOXX first, then pro-rata;
wash rule: same ticker +-30 calendar days, share-for-share, disallowed loss -> replacement basis + holding period; fwd and bwd windows; 2bp/side; price-only returns; BOXX = capital asset (gain on sale).
End wealth = account value minus liquidation tax (all lots, per-lot ST/LT). After-tax CAGR = (liq/600k)^(252/n)-1. wash$ = cumulative disallowed events (chains re-count a loss each time it is re-washed).
Substitute blocked-test: a pending loss sale of the security (>= 0.05% of NAV) within the prior 30 calendar days. Switch-back: see README at bottom. NOT TAX ADVICE.

