11 Nov under S3: TQQQ blocked until 2026-11-29 (30 Oct loss sale, est. -$24k on my reconstruction; owner's Robinhood figure -$31.4k), QLD also blocked (30 Oct loss, est. -$14.8k, buys through 11-29 would wash it). Target D3 = 42.8% TQQQ / 20% VIXY / 37.2% BOXX.
  S3 => QQQ at up to 3x weight, dollar-limited: QQQ 80% (42.8% freed TQQQ dollars + the 37.2% BOXX), VIXY 20%, BOXX 0 => ~0.80x exposure vs 1.28x (shortfall ~0.48x) until 2026-11-30, then switch QQQ -> TQQQ (guard: if QQQ lots are at a loss > 0.05% NAV, hold up to 45 days).
  (VIXY also had its own buy 11-11; VIXM was sold at a gain 11-02/11-05, no VIXY loss pending -> not blocked.)
SWITCH-BACK RULE (guard): when the primary is unblocked (>=31 days after its last pending loss sale) and the target still wants it, sell the substitute and buy the primary, UNLESS the substitute lots are at an unrealized loss > 0.05% of NAV (that sale would create a fresh loss on a ticker the strategy also trades -> likely new wash); then keep the substitute until the loss is gone, the primary target goes to 0, or 45 days pass. 'eager' = always switch on day 31.

